  "text": "proprium.sacratissimi-cordis-iesu-epistola",
  "about": "The Epistle of the feast of the Most Sacred Heart of Jesus, Ephesians 3:8–19. Saint Paul preaches the unsearchable riches of Christ and prays that the faithful may know His love which surpasses all knowledge.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Brethren: To me, the least of all the saints, is given this grace: to preach among the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of Christ, and to enlighten all men as to the dispensation of the mystery hidden from eternity in God, who created all things:" },
    "s02": { "translation": "that the manifold wisdom of God may be made known through the Church to the principalities and powers in heavenly places, according to the eternal purpose which He accomplished in Christ Jesus our Lord, in whom we have boldness and access with confidence through faith in Him." },
    "s03": { "translation": "For this cause I bow my knees to the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, of whom all paternity in heaven and earth is named:" },
    "s04": { "translation": "that He would grant you, according to the riches of His glory, to be strengthened with might by His Spirit unto the inward man, and that Christ may dwell by faith in your hearts:" },
    "s05": { "translation": "that, being rooted and founded in charity, you may be able to comprehend with all the saints what is the breadth and length and height and depth:" },
    "s06": { "translation": "and to know also the charity of Christ which surpasseth knowledge, that you may be filled unto all the fullness of God." }
  },
